  "decision_summary": "The query is a large, extremely lipophilic polyisoprenoid quinone (MW ~863, logP ~17.9, 31 rotatable bonds) with no ionizable groups. The physicochemical prior strongly predicts poor aqueous solubility and absorption, favoring F < 20%. Retrieved experimental evidence comes from small, moderately lipophilic drugs with no structural similarity to the query, so it is not transferable. Therefore, low oral bioavailability is the better-supported prediction, but confidence is low due to the absence of direct experimental evidence for this chemical class.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No experimental bioavailability data for polyisoprenoid quinones or ubiquinone-like compounds.",
    "No evidence on formulation strategies that might improve absorption of such lipophilic molecules.",
    "The physicochemical prior is not a direct experimental measurement of oral bioavailability."
